#!/bin/bash
# Quick-reference cheatsheet. Type `cheatsheet` from any shell on a machine
# running claude-mgr to display this. Symlinked to /usr/local/bin/cheatsheet
# from claude-mgr/cheatsheet in the claudefarm repo.

# Use less if available + interactive, otherwise just cat
PAGER="cat"
if [ -t 1 ] && command -v less >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  PAGER="less -R -F -X"  # -F exits if content fits on one screen, -X disables alt-screen
fi

$PAGER <<'CHEAT'

K12 LXC 105 CHEATSHEET
======================

  Type `cheatsheet` any time to show this.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
TMUX (the terminal multiplexer Claude runs inside)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Default prefix is Ctrl+b. Most commands need it first.

  DETACH (leave Claude running, exit terminal):  Ctrl+b then d
  REATTACH from terminal:                        ssh claude-<instance>
                                                 (or `tmux a -t claude-<x>` here)
  LIST sessions:                                 tmux ls

  SCROLL through history:                        scroll wheel (mouse mode is on)
                                                 OR Ctrl+b [ then PgUp/PgDn, q to exit
  COPY text:                                     click + drag (auto-copies)

  SPLIT pane vertically:                         Ctrl+b then |
  SPLIT pane horizontally:                       Ctrl+b then -
  SWITCH between panes:                          Alt+arrow keys (no prefix needed)
  CLOSE a pane:                                  type `exit` or Ctrl+d

  RELOAD tmux config after editing it:           Ctrl+b then r

  !!! NEVER Ctrl+C inside Claude !!!
  That kills the Claude process. Use Ctrl+b then d to safely detach.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE INSTANCES (managed by `claude-mgr`)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Open the manager TUI:        claude-mgr
  List all instances:          claude-mgr list
  Start a new instance:        claude-mgr start <name> [--workdir /path]
                                                       [--clone <git-url>]
  Restart an instance:         claude-mgr restart <name>
  Stop an instance:            claude-mgr stop <name>
  Show last URL:               claude-mgr url <name>
  Remove an instance:          claude-mgr remove <name> [--purge-workdir]

  Each instance is a separate Claude conversation in its own tmux session
  named `claude-<instance>`. Workdir defaults to /root; pass --workdir to
  point at /data/dev/<repo> instead.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
HOMELAB WIRING
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Repo on this LXC:            /data/dev/claudefarm
  Repo on Windows:             C:\Users\cmoss\github\k12-homelab
  Runbook:                     <repo>/runbook/k12-runbook.md

  Reach Proxmox host:          ssh proxmox        (alias)
  Reach Sound detector Pi:     ssh satellite      (alias)
  Run command in any LXC:      ssh proxmox "pct exec <id> -- <cmd>"

  HA REST API token:           /root/.claude/ha-token
  Test it:
    curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $(cat /root/.claude/ha-token)" \
      https://ha.mossom.co.uk/api/

----------------------------------------------------------------------
HA ANNOUNCE (talk through the user's Google Hubs)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Skill: ~/.claude/skills/ha-announce/SKILL.md

  Quick test:
    TOKEN=$(cat /root/.claude/ha-token)
    curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"message":"Claude on K12 says hi","target":"all"}' \
      https://ha.mossom.co.uk/api/services/script/announce

  target: cabin / living_room / bedroom / all

CHEAT
